  "notes": "The basic pattern is AがBに{依存|いぞん}する (A depends on B). Used both for neutral reliance and for harmful addiction.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- 〜に{依存|いぞん}する: to depend on, to be reliant on\n- {依存|いぞん}{症|しょう}: addiction (as a medical condition)\n- {依存|いぞん}{度|ど}: degree of dependence\n- {依存|いぞん}{体質|たいしつ}: dependent personality/tendency\n- {相互|そうご}{依存|いぞん}: mutual dependence, interdependence\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {頼|たよ}る: to rely on, to depend on — more colloquial and emotional; implies seeking help or support from someone\n- {当|あ}てにする: to count on, to expect — implies relying on someone or something to come through\n- {甘|あま}える: to depend on someone's kindness — implies taking advantage of someone's goodwill\n\nPRONUNCIATION:\nTraditionally read as いそん, but いぞん has become the dominant modern pronunciation. Both are accepted.",
